[
  {
    "number": 56,
    "title": "Expose validated connector geometry for Prism",
    "body": "Existing zone-only caches cannot identify the real connector housings needed for Prism’s flat-face joins. This adds a validated, versioned connector graph while retaining the current wall response and rendering.\n\nRefs #52. The backend owns bounded cache enrichment; invalid layouts retain the prior cache, and graph fields exclude credentials and private state. Controller orientation and Y inversion run in the producer; presentation rotation and flips remain with the browser. No visible UI, installed runtime, or physical-light behavior changes.\n\nValidation at `e49d71e81f3d6c0dedca718c1fb1088c2c7b833a`:\n- Eight focused tests cover the saved 15-Line fixture, alternate topology/orientation, legacy enrichment, privacy, malformed input, atomic failure, bounded retries, and concurrent readers. The new tests failed before implementation for the absent graph/cache contract.\n- All 153 isolated Python tests pass, with both localhost proxy bypass variables set. Workflow validation and all 10 workflow tests pass. The synchronized main spec and completed change are archived on this branch.\n- The preceding implementation revision passed all nine hosted jobs, including browser checks and Windows Python. Current-head PR CI and independent Standards/Specification reviews follow publication.\n- Local browser execution is blocked by Chromium socket restrictions. Browser download is also blocked by the environment’s domain allowlist; hosted browser CI supplies that check.\n\nFixed comparison: base and merge-base `ea3b95661352f927aceaf92b62d74660978c201f`, head `e49d71e81f3d6c0dedca718c1fb1088c2c7b833a`; `git diff ea3b95661352f927aceaf92b62d74660978c201f...e49d71e81f3d6c0dedca718c1fb1088c2c7b833a`. Worktree is clean. Source-only delivery; no installation or physical checks ran. Shared work-guide synchronization is being prepared in a linked Hub companion PR.\n",
    "state": "open",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/jimmie-potts/codex-nanoleaf/pull/56",
